# **Which end-to-end sub-stages a changed path needs** (`Tools/e2e-affected.sh`). One rule a line:
#
#   <pattern>   <what>
#
# <pattern> is a path from the repository's root, matched as a shell pattern (`*` crosses `/`). **The first rule that
# matches decides**, so the specific come before the general. **A path no rule matches selects everything**: an
# unforeseen file costs a full run, never a missed one.
#
# <what> is `none` (no E2E sub-stage reads it), `all`, or sub-stage and stage names (`Tools/e2e-substages.txt`; a stage
# means its default sub-stages). Prefixed `check:`, the path is a check's own code (its analyzer, verdicts, scenario or
# instrument), and each sub-stage named also brings its positive control, from the `control` lines.
#
#   control <sub-stage> <its positive control>

control hostile.production hostile.controls
control hostile.app        hostile.controls
control library.corpus     library.control

# --- What no E2E sub-stage reads: the notes, the other platforms, tests that run only here ---------------------------
*.md                                                none
LICENSE                                             none
dev-docs/*                                          none
apps/android/*                                      none
apps/windows/*                                      none
apps/linux/*                                        none
apps/web/*                                          none
apps/extension/*                                    none
core/xdict-wasm/*                                   none
core/xdict-ffi/test-*.sh                            none
core/xdict-ffi/measure-memory.sh                    none
apps/apple/Tests/*                                  none
apps/apple/Tools/tests/*                            none
apps/apple/Tools/e2e-affected.*                     none
apps/apple/Tools/strings.sh                         none
apps/apple/Tools/compiler-warnings.py               none
apps/apple/Tools/release.sh                         none
apps/apple/Tools/gate-cache.py                      none
apps/apple/.swiftlint.yml                           none

# --- The core: the sample of the owner's dictionaries comes from one of its tests; a crate read only by rendering,
# health or lookup selects those; the rest is in every bundle (2026-10-16: a one-attribute change to xdict-entry ran
# every sub-stage, 46 min) -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
core/xdict-core/tests/entries_corpus.rs             entries.quick
core/xdict-core/examples/index_bench.rs             library.corpus
core/*/tests/*                                      none
core/*/benches/*                                    none
core/xdict-health/*                                 library.health
core/xdict-lookup/*                                 lookup library.corpus
core/xdict-entry/*                                  hostile.production hostile.app hostile.faults hostile.binding reader entries.full entries.persistence lookup.core sound
core/*                                              all
conformance/fixtures/hostile/*                      check:hostile.production hostile.app
conformance/fixtures/twin-*                         check:hostile.binding
conformance/*                                       check:service.conformance

# --- The harness: what runs the checks ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
apps/apple/Tools/hostile/analyze.py                 check:hostile.production hostile.faults hostile.binding reader entries.full entries.persistence entries.lab
apps/apple/Tools/hostile/battery.py                 check:hostile.production hostile.app
apps/apple/Tools/hostile/reader.py                  check:reader
apps/apple/Tools/hostile/pointer.swift              check:reader library.generated
apps/apple/Tools/hostile/*                          check:hostile.production hostile.app reader
apps/apple/Tools/lookup/verdicts.py                 check:hostile.app
apps/apple/Tools/lookup/run-app-hostile.sh          check:hostile.app
apps/apple/Tools/lookup/*                           check:lookup
apps/apple/Tools/anywhere/*                         check:selection services panel menubar shortcut
apps/apple/Tools/library/health-expected.json       check:library.health
apps/apple/Tools/library/*                          check:library.generated library.corpus
apps/apple/Tools/gallery/*                          none
# The harness's shared code: a change to it can break any stage, but most are a line for one stage's driver, which that
# stage's own rule above already selects. So these select a smoke set, a minute in all: the bundle launched, the kit's
# lab, the fixtures, a lookup window over the corpus (2026-10-16: a lookup driver change with three such lines ran every
# sub-stage, 46 min). **A change to what every stage shares (the run's setup, the lock, the evidence, `flunk`) names its
# stages or runs T2.**
apps/apple/Tools/build-lab.sh                       hostile.binding hostile.faults lookup.core
apps/apple/Tools/e2e.sh                             launch service.conformance hostile.binding hostile.faults service.recovery lookup.core
apps/apple/Makefile                                 launch service.conformance hostile.binding hostile.faults service.recovery lookup.core
apps/apple/Tools/build-fixtures.sh                  service library.generated lookup selection services panel menubar shortcut
apps/apple/Tools/*                                  all

